30,2,1,talk,Misaki,,It's clear that weekly routines are collapsing and the car is often left dirty or empty. We need more reliability than we have now.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,May,,"Recording every single run is a nightmare; it takes way too much time. Plus, the usage is totally uneven between weekdays and weekends.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The fixed costs are significant, and the fuel contributions have been very uneven. A simple split is not reflecting the actual usage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"I found out that checking each other's math makes us fight. Also, asking for favors constantly is what ruins these arrangements.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Kenji,,I saw the fuel receipts! Some of us are paying way more than others. And the diary shows we barely use it on Tuesdays but fight over Saturdays.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Takumi, if asking for favors is the problem, maybe we should stop asking and just have set times.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. If we spend an hour a week just recording runs, we're wasting our lives. We need something low-maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Servas,,"If we want to avoid the friction Takumi mentioned, we should move away from ""favors"" and toward a structured agreement.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"I agree. If we keep auditing each other's spending, we're just going to end up apologizing and staying angry.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Kenji,,But we can't just ignore that some people drive way more! We need a way to pay that's fair but doesn't feel like an interrogation.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"A fixed schedule would solve the ""handover"" stress and the collapsing weekly trips. You'd know exactly when it's yours.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,May,,"As long as it doesn't require a spreadsheet and a meeting every Sunday night, I'm in.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A fixed allocation might be too rigid for some, but it removes the need for constant negotiation and ""favors.""","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"If it stops the clipped replies and the tension, I'm for it. Let's avoid the ""checking figures"" trap.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"If we have fixed days, does that mean we pay a fixed amount? That would be so much easier than guessing fuel costs!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Misaki,,It seems we all want less conflict and more predictability.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,May,,I just want my evenings back.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Servas,,Balance is key. We must weigh convenience against absolute mathematical precision.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Takumi,,Let's pick the option that keeps us friends.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready to vote for whatever stops the guesswork!,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
